{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ChannelSeparation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ChannelSeparation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Instanton","lean:module:QOU.Torsion.JetProlongation","lean:module:QOU.GradedFrobeniusHopf","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.channelSeparates_iff_multi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.channelSeparates_iff_multi","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L186-L191","doc":"**Channel-separation activation theorem.**\n`channelSeparates n = true ↔ n ≥ 2` — proved directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.channelSeparates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.channelSeparates","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L178-L184","doc":"**Channel-separation activation predicate.**\nBoolean indicator of whether `n` strands witness\nmulti-generator structure. Defined as `decide (n ≥ 2)` so the\nqualitative fact that channel separation activates exactly for\n`n ≥ 2` is true by definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.kahler_differentials_no_sym_component","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.kahler_differentials_no_sym_component","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L131-L155","doc":"**Proposition**: the Kähler differentials `Ω¹(A)` of the Frobenius--Hopf\nobject have no symmetric (degree-0) component.\n\nIn the Hecke realisation: `Ω¹(A) = ker(μ : A ⊗ A → A)`.\nThe symmetric component of `A ⊗ A` maps surjectively onto `A^{sym}`\nvia `μ`, so `ker(μ)^{sym} = 0`.\n\nThis is a reformulation of the fact that `d(𝟏) = 0` — the differential\nof the identity element vanishes, so the degree-0 piece of the\ndifferential forms is trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.level_to_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.level_to_degree","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L129-L129","doc":"Each jet level k corresponds to Hecke elements of word length ≤ k. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.max_word_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.max_word_length","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L127-L127","doc":"The jet level ≤ maximal word length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.n","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L125-L125","doc":"The number of Hecke generators (= number of strands minus 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L123-L123","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HeckeJetCorrespondence","kind":"structure","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L101-L129","doc":"The **Hecke--jet correspondence**: the word-length filtration on\n`H_n(q)` corresponds to the jet level filtration on `J^k(A)`.\n\n| Jet level | Hecke degree | Elements |\n|-----------|-------------|----------|\n| `J^0(A)` | degree 0 | identity `𝟏` |\n| `J^1(A)` | degree 1 | single generators `σ_i` |\n| `J^k(A)` | degree ≤ k | words of length ≤ k in `σ_i` |\n\nThe kernel of `j^1 : J^1(A) → J^0(A) = A` is `Ω¹(A)`, which\ncorresponds to the degree-1 piece of the Hecke algebra (the\ngenerators modulo the identity).\n\nIn the graded decomposition:\n- `Ω¹(A)^{sym} = 0` (the symmetric component of the differential\n  forms vanishes, since `d(1) = 0` in the symmetric representation)\n- `Ω¹(A)^{std}` = the standard representation piece (degree 1)\n\nThis is why the 6×6 transfer matrix (which tracks ALL irreps) gives\nno new information per generator — but multi-generator products\n(corresponding to higher jet levels) DO separate the channels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.jet_compatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.jet_compatible","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L97-L97","doc":"The jet object's Frobenius--Hopf data matches the grading's. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.grading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.grading","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L95-L95","doc":"The base is a graded Frobenius--Hopf object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.jet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.jet","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L93-L93","doc":"The categorical jet data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading.mk","kind":"ctor","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetFiltrationPreservesGrading","kind":"structure","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L78-L97","doc":"The **jet filtration** on the graded Frobenius--Hopf object.\n\nAt each jet level `k`, the grading `A = A^0 ⊕ A^{≥1}` induces\na grading on `J^k(A)`:\n- `J^k(A)^0 = J^k(A^0)` (jet prolongation of the symmetric component)\n- `J^k(A)^{≥1} = J^k(A^{≥1})` (jet prolongation of the high component)\n\nThe compatibility condition ensures that the jet evaluation\n`j^k : J^k(A) → J^{k-1}(A)` respects the grading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.adjoint_vanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.adjoint_vanishing","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L74-L74","doc":"Adjoint vanishing at the base level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.adjointObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.adjointObj","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The adjoint object at the base level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.base","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The base graded Frobenius--Hopf object (level 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.JetGradedChannelSeparation","kind":"structure","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ChannelSeparation.lean#L57-L74","doc":"**Jet-graded channel separation data**: a graded Frobenius--Hopf\nobject at each jet level, with the grading compatible with\nthe jet prolongation structure.\n\nAt each level `k`:\n- `A_k = J^k(A)` has a graded decomposition `A_k = A_k^0 ⊕ A_k^{≥1}`\n- The jet evaluation `j^k : J^k(A) → J^{k-1}(A)` preserves the grading\n- The adjoint vanishing `Hom(𝟙, Ad(A_k)) = 0` holds at all levels ","signatureChunk":0}]}